# omp-base.packages -- what omp-install pacstraps.
#
# Derived from upstream Omarchy's install/omarchy-base.packages and the
# applicable rows of install/omarchy-other.packages. The upstream files stay
# the source of truth; this is the ppc64le projection of them. Lines starting
# with '#' are comments; the clip list with reasons is in omp-clipped.packages.
#
# Nothing here is a guess about whether a package exists: omp-install resolves
# the whole list against the configured repositories with `pacman -Sp` before
# it touches the disk, and refuses to partition if a name does not resolve.

# --- system base -------------------------------------------------------------
autoconf-archive
base
base-devel
linux-firmware
btrfs-progs
e2fsprogs
dosfstools
dotnet-runtime
exfatprogs
mkinitcpio
# libxkbcommon is listed explicitly, not left to dependency resolution:
# Arch POWER's kbd 2.10.0-1 links /usr/bin/loadkeys against libxkbcommon.so.0
# but its depends= still says only glibc/gzip/pam. mkinitcpio's sd-vconsole
# hook pulls loadkeys in, so on a target that has nothing else dragging
# libxkbcommon in, `mkinitcpio -P` fails with
#   ERROR: binary dependency 'libxkbcommon.so.0' not found for 'loadkeys'
# and the machine gets no initramfs. Measured in the QEMU rig. This line can go
# once kbd's depends= is fixed upstream.
libxkbcommon
sudo
networkmanager
openssh
git
less
man-db
inetutils
socat
jq
unzip
zram-generator

# The kernel is NOT listed here. omp-install adds it from --kernel/OMP_KERNEL_PKG
# (default linux-power9) so the one package that differs per build stays a
# single variable rather than a line buried in a manifest.

# --- Omarchy proper ----------------------------------------------------------
omarchy
omarchy-settings
omarchy-nvim
# The theme is listed in iso/profile/packages.ppc64le too, but that is the LIVE
# medium. Listing it there does nothing for the installed system, and no
# package depends on it (the omarchy package ships upstream's themes; ours are
# separate). omarchy-theme-powerpc carries the two generic PowerPC themes the
# stock install ships. omarchy-theme-power9 (OpenPOWER / POWER9 branding) is
# deliberately not installed by default; `pacman -S omarchy-theme-power9` adds it.
omarchy-theme-powerpc
# The screensaver's animation engine. omarchy-launch-screensaver opens with
# `omarchy-cmd-missing ttfx && exit 1`, so without it the idle screensaver at
# 150s silently does nothing -- no error, no notification, nothing to debug.
# Omarchy publishes ttfx from their own repository, which neither Arch POWER
# nor Arch carries, so ours/ttfx/ in the packaging tree is our own
# recipe built from upstream Rust. No porting was needed, only packaging.
ttfx
hyprland
hyprland-guiutils
hyprland-preview-share-picker
hyprpicker
hyprsunset
quickshell
uwsm
sddm
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-terminal-exec
wireplumber
pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
pipewire-pulse
gst-plugin-pipewire
gtk4-layer-shell
qt6-wayland
